# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One bard song per walk pass, Discordance, Peacemaking and Provocation in turn.
#
# @ hotkeys Cancel Current Target
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__song_next
#      Which song plays next: 1 discordance, 2 peacemaking, 3 provocation. Literal values,
#      since Razor has no arithmetic.
#
#   var__song_after
#      Scratch: the song after the one just played.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if not varexist var__song_next
    @setvar! var__song_next 1
endif
@setvar! var__song_after 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ loop
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # BARD SONG
    #
    # Three 15 minute AoE buffs, each worth 8.5% at this Effective Barding, landing on the
    # player and every follower in range. Sung on the walk between pulls, never in a
    # fight: while engaged, Discordance and Peacemaking keep Music busy so a song rarely
    # gets a window, and playing an instrument interrupts a spell already in flight.
    #
    # Singing on the walk is what removes follower tracking from this script. A resummoned
    # creature picks the songs up on the next walk, so nothing has to notice that it died.
    #
    # findbuff is deliberately NOT the gate. The buffs run 15 minutes, so a findbuff test
    # would be true almost always and the refresh would never fire. The gate is the song
    # cooldown plus the slot each song borrows.
    #
    # A branch only advances var__song_next once the cursor was actually delivered, so a
    # song that could not go out, for any reason, is retried next pass instead of being
    # skipped.
    #
    # The chain only picks the skill and the song after it, the three share the rest.
    # The song goes on the ground under you, the way the wiki (Musicianship) starts one:
    # it reaches you, every follower and anyone green to you within 50 tiles, and a
    # ground target leaves lastharmful alone (user check, 2026-10-20). The backpack it
    # used to target answers a harmful cursor, which moved lastharmful off the pick
    # (document/scripting/razor.md part 3), so the song had to stand down around a pick.
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if cooldown "song" = 0 and cooldown "music" = 0 and not warmode and var__instrument_ok = 1 and var__my_instrument != 0 and not targetexists and not casting
        @setvar! var__song_after 0

        if var__song_next = 1 and skill "Discordance" > 0 and cooldown "disco" = 0
            useskill 'Discordance'
            @setvar! var__song_after 2
        elseif var__song_next = 2 and skill "Peacemaking" > 0 and cooldown "peace/provo" = 0
            useskill 'Peacemaking'
            @setvar! var__song_after 3
        elseif var__song_next = 3 and skill "Provocation" > 0 and cooldown "peace/provo" = 0
            useskill 'Provocation'
            @setvar! var__song_after 1
        endif

        if var__song_after != 0
            waitfortarget wait__bard_target

            if insysmsg "What instrument shall you play"
                target var__my_instrument
                waitfortarget wait__bard_target

                if insysmsg "That is not a musical instrument"
                    @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
                endif
            endif

            if targetexists
                targetrelloc 0 0
                @setvar! var__song_next var__song_after
            endif
        endif
    endif
